From 1d95c1604099a3e99cdac3bd0517762283ba5329 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jetson <jetson@orin-nano.tail52323b.ts.net>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:04:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] nv_attach: the thread-local area by value where its
 probes allow it

A kernel whose probe functions reach the thread-local area (1530) only
through constant-key lookups and 32-bit loads and stores with 64-bit
registers keeps the area (at most 16 bytes) in a .local slot of its own
and passes its 8-byte words by value: a probe function that accesses the
area takes them as .param inputs, one that writes it also returns them.
Inside, the area is .b32 halves, a lookup the non-null constant 1, a load
cvt.u64.u32 and a store cvt.u32.u64 of its half; the halves are packed and
returned before every ret. The kernel loads the words before each call
and stores what a writing function returns (with the call's predicate).

Eligibility is an allowlist, decided once per probe function
(plan_by_value) and used by both the kernel and the function rewrite:
every map helper call must name its map with a constant; a thread-local
map may only be looked up, with a constant key the program just stored
(forwarded_key, a single mov of a plain decimal), in range; every statement
the tokenizer finds mentioning a lookup's result must be its definition, a
compare with 0, or such an access inside the value, unguarded, on a line of
its own; every ret on a line of its own. Anything else in any probe
function of a kernel keeps the area in memory for that kernel, with the
reason logged ("Thread-local area kept in memory"). Map calls with a
constant fd of another type get 0 for the area (helpers 1-3 read it for
thread-local maps only). A kernel none of whose probes reaches the area
gets no area at all.

Basis: .local is the thread's own (PTX ISA 5.1.5) and the area's address
never leaves the rewritten accesses; device function inputs and returns
are .param, returns written with st.param (5.1.6.4, 7.1); ld/st with a
wider register zero-extend a load and store the low bits (9.4.1), as
cvt.u64.u32 and cvt.u32.u64 do (6.5.1). The halves' order in a word is
packed and unpacked only by this code.

Measured first as a hand-written form of n70's lat_mmvq PTX (passes v1/v2,
tg128, mul_mat_vec_q probed): 0.021-0.024 ns per thread less than the area
in memory, 54.3 -> 55.9 t/s; the built pass emits that text byte for byte.
pt_victim: seven tools exact as before (lat by value; carry and tlatomic
keep the area: carry stores its keys with one vector store, so they are not
forwarded; tlatomic's area is 24 bytes) and a new one-value carry tool
(carry1) by value, 0 mismatches over 3.88M thread executions; with the
halves swapped in one exit (override) it reports every exit of that kernel.
Unit tests: [tl-byvalue], 7 cases. The sum-map test whose probe does not
use its thread-local map now expects no area (nothing to pass).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
